course: dictionary
lesson: 2352
title: Short forms: ct and CT
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: ct is not a word you say out loud. It is an abbreviation, a short form of a longer word, and writers use it to save space. What it means depends on where you see it: on a ring it is about gold, on a price it is about cents, and on a letter it is about a court.
explain: Look at the clues around it. «18 ct gold» is on jewellery, so ct is a measure of how pure gold is. In «50 ct», the small price tells you the money is in cents. In «12 Oak Ct», it sits in an address, so Ct is short for Court.
explain: Capital letters can change the meaning too. CT, in capitals, is a different short form. Read this sentence: «Anyone knocked out, even briefly, should be checked by a doctor; hospitals sometimes do a CT scan, a special 3D X-ray, of the head.» Here CT is a medical scan, not gold or money. Always check the context before you decide.
fact: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer word or phrase.
fact: «ct» can mean carat, the unit for the weight of diamonds and gems (1 carat = 0.2 grams).
fact: «ct» can also mean karat, which measures how pure gold is: 24 ct means pure gold.
fact: «ct» can mean cent or cents in prices, as in «50 ct»; «Ct» can mean Court in addresses, as in «12 Oak Ct».
fact: «CT» can mean computed tomography, a CT scan, which is an X-ray that makes pictures of slices inside the body; it is also the postal code for Connecticut, a state in the USA.
exercise: On a ring it says «18 ct gold». What does ct mean here? | A type of cake | A street name | The number of days it has been made | * A measure of how pure the gold is
exercise: A price label says «50 ct». What does ct mean? | Computed tomography | * Cents | Court | Carats
exercise: A letter is addressed to «12 Oak Ct». What does Ct stand for? | Cent | Connecticut | Carat | * Court
test: In «a CT scan, a special 3D X-ray, of the head», what is a CT scan? | A cent price on a bag | A street in a town | * An X-ray scan that makes pictures of slices inside the body | A measure of gold
test: Which short form is the postal code for a US state? | ct | * CT | 18 ct | Ct
exam: Why do «18 ct gold» and «a CT scan» mean different things, even though both use the letters c and t? | Because they are spelt the same and mean the same thing | Because CT is only ever used in maths | * Because the context and the capital letters show which short form is being used | Because ct is a real word with many meanings, so it changes by mood
